    "result_text": "BUILD SUCCESS \u2014 all tests pass. Here's a summary of the change.\n\n## Summary\n\nAdded an optional `email` field to owners: when present it must be syntactically valid, is stored/returned lower-cased, and an invalid value is rejected with 400.\n\n**Changes made:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added an optional `email` property (`type: string`, `format: email`, `maxLength: 255`) to the `OwnerFields` schema. Since the generator has `performBeanValidation`, this emits a `@Email` constraint on the generated `OwnerFieldsDto`, and the field flows into `OwnerDto` for responses.\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added the `email` column (`@Column(name = \"email\")`) with getter/setter.\n\n3. **`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 In `addOwner` (and `updateOwner` for consistency), when `email` is present it's trimmed, lower-cased, and validated against a syntactic pattern (`^[^\\s@]+@[^\\s@]+\\.[^\\s@]+$`); invalid \u2192 `400 Bad Request`. The normalized value is what gets persisted. MapStruct maps `email` between DTO and entity automatically.\n\n4. **Schema DDL** (`db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`) \u2014 Added the `email` column to the `owners` table. This is required because the hsqldb profile used by tests runs with `ddl-auto=none`.\n\n5. **Seed data** (`db/hsqldb/data.sql`, `db/mysql/data.sql`) \u2014 These used positional `INSERT INTO owners VALUES (...)`, which broke with the new column, so I appended a `NULL` email to each seed owner. (h2/postgres already used explicit column lists and needed no change.)\n\n**Test results:** The three new acceptance tests (`coreLowercasesEmail`, `errorRejectsInvalidEmail`, `functionalityAcceptsMissingEmail`) and the full suite pass \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\nNote: validation is enforced both by the generated `@Email` bean-validation constraint and the controller's explicit check; the controller additionally performs the lower-casing normalization that bean validation alone doesn't do.",
